# LocalFit - Fitness Tracker App

## Technology Stack
- **Framework**: Avalonia UI (cross-platform .NET UI framework)
- **MVVM**: CommunityToolkit.Mvvm (ObservableObject, RelayCommand)
- **Database**: Entity Framework Core with SQLite
- **Icons**: Lucide.Avalonia
- **Language**: C# with nullable reference types enabled

## Architecture Patterns

### MVVM Pattern
- ViewModels inherit from `ObservableObject` (CommunityToolkit.Mvvm)
- Use `[ObservableProperty]` for properties that need to notify changes
- Use `[RelayCommand]` for commands
- ViewModels are in `LocalFit/ViewModels/`
- Views are in `LocalFit/Views/`
- Models are in `LocalFit.Lib/DataBase/`

### Code Style
- Use partial classes for ViewModels with source generators
- Use `using var db = new UserContext()` for database access (disposes automatically)
- Prefer async/await for database operations
- Use compiled bindings with `x:DataType` in XAML
- Enable nullable reference types - handle nulls explicitly

### Database Access
- Always use `using var db = new UserContext()` pattern
- Use `Include()` for eager loading related entities
- Use `FindAsync()` for single entity lookups
- Use `ToListAsync()` for collections
- Save changes with `await db.SaveChangesAsync()`

## UI/UX Guidelines

### Mobile-First Design
- Design for mobile screens first (narrow viewport)
- Use responsive layouts (Grid with ColumnDefinitions/RowDefinitions)
- Minimum touch target size: 44px height
- Use larger fonts and spacing for mobile readability

### Dialogs
- Use in-app overlay dialogs (UserControl with ZIndex), NOT separate windows
- Dialogs should have backdrop (Rectangle with opacity)
- Dialog borders: `BorderBrush="#222222"` and `BorderThickness="2"`
- Typical dialog size: Width="400", MaxHeight="600"
- Use Grid.RowSpan to cover all rows when showing overlay

### Controls
- Use `NumericUpDown` with `ShowButtonSpinner="False"` for numeric inputs (not TextBox)
- Use `ComboBox` for dropdowns (set MinHeight="44" for mobile)
- Use `TextBox` for text input
- Use `LucideIcon` for icons instead of text where appropriate
- Buttons: MinHeight="44", use icons for Save (Check) and Cancel (X)

### Color Scheme
- **Primary Colors**: Black/White monochrome scheme
  - Dark gray: `#222222` (primary dark color for backgrounds, borders, text on light backgrounds)
  - Light gray: `#DDDDDD` (primary light color for backgrounds, text on dark backgrounds)
  - White: `#FFFFFF` (text on dark backgrounds when needed)
- **Warning Colors**: Red/Yellow only for warnings
  - Red: `#FFE53935` - **ONLY** used when calories exceed goal (text color, not background)
  - Yellow: Reserved for future warning use
- **Theme-Aware Icons**: Use `{DynamicResource SystemControlForegroundBaseHighBrush}` for edit/delete icons to automatically adapt to light/dark themes
- **Backgrounds**: 
  - Dark backgrounds: `#222222` for cards, buttons, headers
  - Light backgrounds: `#DDDDDD` for light areas, info boxes
  - Transparent: For ListBox controls
- **Borders**: `#222222` for all borders
- **Text Colors**:
  - On dark backgrounds (`#222222`): Use `#DDDDDD` or `#FFFFFF`
  - On light backgrounds (`#DDDDDD`): Use `#222222`
  - Calories warning: Use `#FFE53935` for text when calories exceed goal (background stays `#222222`)
- **No Other Colors**: Remove all green, blue, orange, purple colors. Only black/white/gray with red for calorie warnings.

### Styling
- Global styles defined in `App.axaml`
- Use `Classes="SaveButton"` for primary action buttons (black `#222222` background with `#DDDDDD` text)
- Button text/icons should be centered (HorizontalContentAlignment/VerticalContentAlignment)
- Use consistent spacing and margins (typically 10-20px)

### Navigation
- Bottom navigation bar with icons
- Use ContentControl with DataTemplates for view switching
- Default view should be the most frequently used (DayTracker)

## Naming Conventions
- ViewModels: `*ViewModel.cs` (e.g., `DayTrackerViewModel`)
- Views: `*View.axaml` (e.g., `DayTrackerView.axaml`)
- Dialogs: `*Dialog.axaml` in `Views/Dialogs/`
- Commands: `*Command` (e.g., `ShowAddFoodDialogCommand`)
- Properties: PascalCase
- Private fields: camelCase (if needed, usually use properties)

## Common Patterns

### ViewModel Property Change Handling
```csharp
partial void OnPropertyNameChanged(Type value)
{
    // Handle property change
}
```

### Dialog Management
- Use `IsDialogVisible` boolean property
- Use `DialogViewModel` property for dialog data context
- Setup dialog with event handlers before showing
- Hide dialog by setting `IsDialogVisible = false` and `DialogViewModel = null`

### Collection Filtering
- Keep full collection in private field
- Use ObservableCollection for filtered/bound collection
- Filter on search text changes using partial method

### Nutrition Calculations
- For Gram100 units: values are per 100g, multiply by (Amount / 100)
- For Piece units: values are per piece, multiply by Amount directly
- Always calculate based on selected preset's unit type

## Best Practices
- Keep ViewModels focused on single responsibility
- Extract repetitive logic into private helper methods
- Use computed properties for derived values (TotalCalories, etc.)
- Handle null cases explicitly (use null-conditional operators or checks)
- Use fire-and-forget pattern `_ = Task.Run()` when needed (with comment)
- Prefer data binding over code-behind
- Use converters for complex binding transformations

## File Organization
- `LocalFit.Lib/` - Shared library (models, database, calculations)
- `LocalFit/ViewModels/` - All ViewModels
- `LocalFit/Views/` - All Views
- `LocalFit/Views/Dialogs/` - Dialog UserControls
- `LocalFit/App.axaml` - Global styles and resources

## Common Gotchas
- Avalonia doesn't support percentage values for MaxWidth/MaxHeight (use fixed pixels)
- Grid doesn't support BorderBrush directly - wrap in Border control
- ContentControl can only have one Content - use DataTemplates for multiple views
- Remember to include namespace declarations (xmlns:lucide, xmlns:vm, etc.)
- Use `x:DataType` for compiled bindings performance
